  "configuration_id": "config_042",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) achieved 63.2% accuracy, giving a single baseline. The most uncertain and potentially high-impact design choice is the image encoder: ResNet50 is a relatively modest CNN, while ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L is substantially more expressive and better suited for cellular morphology. Question: config_042 changes only the image encoder (resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l) while holding all other variables (scvi_n200, avgpool, concat, multiprofile) constant, giving a clean single-variable test of whether a stronger image encoder lifts validation accuracy. Why this is the best next experiment: with 8 experiments remaining, identifying whether the image encoder is a critical bottleneck determines whether subsequent experiments should prioritize ViT-based configurations. A large gain would justify exploring ViT + transformer aggregation + scgpt combinations; a small gain would redirect effort toward RNA encoder or aggregation choices. This single-variable comparison maximizes information per experiment under the limited budget."
